 ```
 
+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to get multiple parts instead of a single rounded unit.
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h 30m"
+ms(90061000, { compound: true })      // "1d 1h 1m 1s"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h 30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })          // "1s"
+```
+
+Compound output uses days, hours, minutes and seconds only (so longer spans are shown in days, e.g. `400d`), skips zero-valued parts, and drops leftover milliseconds. Values under one second are shown as `0s`. The option is ignored when `long` is `true`.
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
